  "description": "Comodo Dome Firewall 2.7.0 contains a reflected cross-site scripting vulnerability that allows attackers to inject malicious scripts by submitting unsanitized input through the NTP_SERVER_LIST parameter. Attackers can send POST requests to the /korugan/time endpoint with script payloads in the NTP_SERVER_LIST parameter to execute arbitrary JavaScript in users' browsers.",
